course: dictionary
lesson: 5943
title: Massage: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Massage can mean rubbing someone's body to ease sore muscles, or it can mean changing numbers. «She had a foot massage after the football match.» Feet and rubbing point to the body meaning.
explain: Massage can also be a verb: «The physio massaged his injured leg.» Here someone is doing the rubbing, so the word is a verb. Ask yourself: is this something someone does with their hands, or a change to facts?
explain: The third meaning is informal and negative. «Businesses massage the numbers» means they change figures a little dishonestly so they look better than they really are. The word is not about hands at all. Check: if you swap in "change", does the sentence still make sense? If so, you have the right meaning.
fact: Massage means rubbing and pressing someone's body to relax the muscles or ease pain.
fact: As a verb, to massage someone is to give them a massage.
fact: «Massaging the numbers» means changing data so it looks better than it really is.
fact: Officials sometimes say a claim was «not entirely accurate» instead of «false», which is a softer way of saying something is wrong.
fact: Useful phrases: foot massage, massage therapist, massage the figures.
exercise: «She booked a foot massage to relax after the long race.» What does massage mean here? | *To rub and press the feet to ease tired muscles | To count the steps she ran | To change the time on a clock
exercise: A news report says a company «massaged the figures» before the meeting. What does this mean? | It added up the numbers very quickly | *It changed the numbers dishonestly to look better | It cleaned the numbers with a soft cloth | It rubbed the paper flat
exercise: «The physio massaged his injured knee gently.» Which meaning fits best? | To ask a question about his knee | To hide the knee under a blanket | To change facts to look better | *To rub and press a body part to ease pain
test: Which phrase means changing numbers dishonestly? | *Massage the figures | Foot massage | Massage therapist | Give a massage
test: «A massage therapist says, "Lie down and relax."» What is her job? | *To give massages that ease tight muscles | To teach maths in a school | To count numbers in a report | To make food in a restaurant
exam: «Massaging the numbers» in a report means | Rubbing the paper to make it soft | Adding numbers very quickly | Printing the numbers in bold | *Changing data so it looks better than it really is
